{"name":"Crazy Horse","hex":"#a57648","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crazy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of unsound mind; insane; demented. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Out of control."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crazy"},{"term":"horse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hoofed mammal, Equus ferus caballus, often used throughout history for riding and draft work.","Any member of the species Equus ferus, including the Przewalski's horse and the extinct Equus ferus ferus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of horse around.","To play mischievous pranks on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crazy Horse","blocks":[{"text":"Crazy Horse was a Lakota war leader of the Oglala band and one of the most renowned Native American figures of the nineteenth century. Known for his commitment to defending Lakota lands and lifeways, he emerged as a central figure in the northern Great Plains during a period of intense conflict with the United States. Crazy Horse resisted U.S. expansion into the Powder River Country, rejecting treaty settlements and reservation life, and became widely respected for both his tactical skill and his personal humility, which included a lifelong avoidance of being photographed."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Horse","wikidata":"Q44555"},{"title":"Crazy Horse (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Crazy Horse is an American rock band best known for their association with the musician Neil Young. Since 1969, fifteen studio albums and eight live albums have been billed as being by Neil Young and Crazy Horse. They have also released six studio albums of their own between 1971 and 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG/330px-Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Horse_(band)","wikidata":"Q951532"},{"title":"Horse","blocks":[{"text":"The horse is a domesticated, one-toed, hoofed mammal. It belongs to the taxonomic family Equidae and is one of two extant subspecies of Equus ferus. The horse has evolved over the past 45 to 55 million years from a small multi-toed creature, Eohippus, into the large single-toed animal of today, originally in North America. Humans began domesticating horses around 4000 BCE in Central Asia, primarily associated with the Botai culture; their domestication is believed to have been widespread by 3000 BCE. However, contemporary genetic evidence indicates that modern domesticated breeds do not descend from this lineage, instead pointing to the Western Eurasian steppes in the lower Volga-Don region as the homeland of modern domestic horses. The modern horse breed replaced the local populations through their rapid expansion across Eurasia from 2000 BCE. Horses in the subspecies caballus are domesticated, although some domesticated populations live in the wild as feral horses. These feral populations are not true wild horses, which are horses that have never been domesticated. There is an extensive, specialized vocabulary used to describe equine-related concepts, covering everything from anatomy to life stages, size, colors, markings, breeds, locomotion, and behavior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg/330px-Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse","wikidata":"Q726"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7b/Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg/250px-Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7b/Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg/250px-Crazy_Horse_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrazy_Horse_drawing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Crazy_horse_c1877.jpg/500px-Crazy_horse_c1877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Crazy_horse_c1877.jpg/500px-Crazy_horse_c1877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's rendering of Crazy Horse and his band of Oglala on their way from Camp Sheridan to surrender to General Crook at Red Cloud Agency","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrazy_horse_c1877.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Ftrob_ch.JPG/500px-Ftrob_ch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Ftrob_ch.JPG/1280px-Ftrob_ch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Ftrob_ch.JPG/500px-Ftrob_ch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A monument dedicated to Crazy Horse's memory. Although Crazy Horse was never named a Chief, he was honored as a Shirt Wearer.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFtrob_ch.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Crazy_Horse_1877.jpg/500px-Crazy_Horse_1877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Crazy_Horse_1877.jpg/500px-Crazy_Horse_1877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alleged photo of Crazy Horse in 1877; a claim that contradicts the available evidence about the Lakota chief's appearance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrazy_Horse_1877.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/CrazyHorse.jpg/500px-CrazyHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/CrazyHorse.jpg/1280px-CrazyHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/CrazyHorse.jpg/500px-CrazyHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Crazy Horse Memorial in 2020","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrazyHorse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG/500px-Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG/500px-Crazy_Horse_1972.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrazy_Horse_1972.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg/500px-Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg/500px-Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANokota_Horses_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Points_of_a_horse.jpg/500px-Points_of_a_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p